    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1007-a1">

                <pb facs="1023" n="903" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg903"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs to Minister Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte,<lb/>Ministry for Foreign
                            Affairs</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July 26,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">note verbale</hi>.</p>
                <p>The agents of the American Bible Society indulge in Turkey in the spreading of
                    religious books by selling them by means of persuasion in the streets and public
                    places at very low prices (prix dérisoire) and even giving them away gratis.</p>
                <p>As colportage with the object of religious propaganda can not be permitted, the
                    Imperial Government has decided to prohibit it in the future.</p>
                <p>Having the honor of bringing this decision to the attention of the United States
                    legation, the ministry for foreign affairs requests that it will be good enough
                    to so inform those interested.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
